            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Galium elongatum (marsh bedstraw or tall bedstraw) is a species of plants in the Rubiaceae. It is widespread across most of Europe, North Africa and the Middle East from Turkey to Palestine to Iran."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Galium elongatum is a tall, erect herb with panicles of small white flowers."
